    "title": "Scaramucci Sees a 'Second Chance' as Bitcoin Erases Gains Since Trump's November 2024 Election Victory - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Aniket Verma ,\n35 minutes ago\nPhoto Courtesy: Al Teich on Shutterstock.com\nBitcoin’s (CRYPTO: BTC) latest pullback offers investors who missed the last bull run another chance to get in, SkyBridge Capital founder Anthony Scaramucci said on Thursday.\nTime to Buy the Dip?\nScaramucci shared an image comparing Bitcoin’s price at exactly $76,000 on Nov. 5, 2024—after Donald Trump won the presidency—and at the same price on Nov. 5, 2026, after Democrats won the midterm elections.\nThe song features lyrics like, “We’re gonna take Dogecoin to the moon, making this crypto mean $1 soon.\"\n“You have been given a second chance,” Scaramucci wrote, accompanied by a rocket emoji, often used by cryptocurrency enthusiasts to express confidence that prices will rise.\nWhat Happens in the Long Term?\n“Rich Dad Poor Dad” author Robert Kiyosaki also viewed the correction as another buying opportunity , adding that rising global debt, particularly in the U.S., will drive investors toward Bitcoin, gold and silver.\nNotably, Arthur Hayes, Chief Investment Officer at Maelstrom Fund , expects central banks worldwide to eventually print money to head off a broader financial crisis, a policy response he deemed “glorious” for Bitcoin holders.\nBitcoin in Trump 2.0\nBitcoin and the broader cryptocurrency market experienced an initial massive wave of optimism after Trump assumed power. It crossed the $100,000 milestone for the first time in December 2024.\nTrump’s tariff policies pressured Bitcoin in early 2025, but it recovered in the latter part of the year, reaching an all-time high of $126,080.\nIn 2026, broader macro pressures from the Iran war and fading liquidity reversed these gains.\nPrice Action : As of this writing, BTC is down 5.7% in the last 24 hours to $75,681, according to Benzinga Pro.\nPhoto Courtesy: Al Teich on Shutterstock.com\nAdd to Preferred Sources\n1",
    "summary": "Photo Courtesy: Al Teich on Shutterstock.com Bitcoin’s (CRYPTO: BTC) latest pullback offers investors who missed the last bull run another chance to get in, SkyBridge Capital founder Anthony Scaramucci said on Thursday. “You have been given a second chance,” Scaramucci wrote, accompanied by a rocket emoji, often used by cryptocurrency enthusiasts to express confidence that prices will rise. Notably, Arthur Hayes, Chief Investment Officer at Maelstrom Fund , expects central banks worldwide to eventually print money to head off a broader financial crisis, a policy response he deemed “glorious” for Bitcoin holders.",
